<section class="hero" id="home">
<div class="hero-copy">
<p class="eyebrow">Decision Integrity · Procurement Exposure · Supplier Risk · Executive Defensibility</p>
<h1>Can your procurement decision survive pressure?</h1>
<p class="lead"><strong>Supplier failure rarely begins when the supplier fails.</strong></p>
<p class="lead">It begins when the organisation accepts dependency, cost pressure, weak evidence or unclear ownership — and cannot defend the decision later.</p>
<p class="lead">Sovereign Decision Science™ helps leaders expose fragile decisions before they become operational, financial or board-level consequences.</p>
<p class="lead hero-question"><strong>Is the decision defensible before the consequence appears?</strong></p>
<p class="hero-proof-line"><strong>Core line:</strong> Supplier failure begins before the supplier fails. It begins with a decision nobody can defend later.</p>
<div class="hero-actions">
<a class="btn btn-gold" href="#subscribe" title="Go to the free Procurement Exposure Test">Get the Free Procurement Exposure Test™</a>
<a class="btn btn-outline" href="#decision-blind-spot-series" title="Explore The Decision Blind Spot Series">Explore the Decision Blind Spot Series™</a>
<a class="btn btn-outline" href="#premium-review" title="Go to the Premium Written Review">Request Premium Written Review</a>
</div>
</div>
<figure class="hero-visual"><img alt="Procurement exposure and decision integrity under pressure." decoding="async" loading="lazy" src="assets/img_001_af590948d72894b9.webp"/></figure>
</section>
<div class="marquee"><div>Ferreira Doctrine™ · Sovereign Decision Science™ · Procurement Exposure · Decision Integrity · Supplier Exposure · Contract Discipline · Board Scrutiny · Institutional Licensing · Formal Written Engagement · Premium Written Review · Ferreira Doctrine™ · Sovereign Decision Science™ · Procurement Exposure · Decision Integrity · Supplier Exposure · Contract Discipline · Board Scrutiny · Institutional Licensing · Formal Written Engagement · Premium Written Review · </div></div>

<section class="lead-magnet lead-magnet-top" id="subscribe">
<span id="lead-magnet" aria-hidden="true"></span>
<span id="lead-magnet-top" aria-hidden="true"></span>

<p class="eyebrow">Free Executive Test</p>
<h2>Find the procurement decision that may fail later.</h2>

<p>A free public-layer checklist for leaders, procurement teams, supply chain professionals and executives who want to identify supplier, contract, continuity or sourcing decisions that may become difficult to defend under pressure.</p>

<p><strong>The question is not whether the supplier failed. The question is whether the decision that selected, accepted or depended on that supplier was defensible.</strong></p>

<div class="free-test-list">
  <div class="free-test-item">Supplier dependency</div>
  <div class="free-test-item">Weak ownership</div>
  <div class="free-test-item">Cost pressure</div>
  <div class="free-test-item">Missing evidence</div>
  <div class="free-test-item">Emergency buying exposure</div>
  <div class="free-test-item">Continuity assumptions</div>
  <div class="free-test-item">Contract fragility</div>
  <div class="free-test-item">Board-level defensibility risk</div>
</div>

<p class="selection-note">
<strong>Start here:</strong> take the free Procurement Exposure Test™ before choosing a briefing, bundle, premium review or licensing route.
</p>

<div class="cta-row">
  <a class="btn btn-gold" href="https://preview.mailerlite.io/forms/2493615/192272626574427389/share" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Get the Free Test</a>
  <a class="btn btn-outline" href="#product-decision-blind-spot-starter-bundle">View Starter Bundle</a>
  <a class="btn btn-outline" href="#premium-review">Request Premium Review</a>
</div>

<p class="small-note">This is not a diagnostic tool, legal opinion, consulting engagement or implementation system. It is a public-layer entry test designed to help readers recognise exposure before choosing the next route.</p>
<p class="small-note">Public products provide reading access only. Implementation, training, software, AI/LLM ingestion, dashboards, workflows and institutional use require formal written licensing.</p>
</section>

<section class="choice-route" id="choice-route">
  <div class="choice-route-inner">
    <div class="choice-route-head">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Start Here</p>
        <h2>Choose the exposure before you choose the product.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>Most visitors do not need the full catalogue first. They need to identify the decision exposure in front of them and select the smallest adequate public-layer product.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="route-cards">
      <a class="route-card primary" href="#product-decision-blind-spot-starter-bundle" title="Go to the recommended first purchase"><span class="route-tag">Recommended first purchase</span><h3>Procurement or supplier exposure</h3><p>Supplier delays, emergency buying, cheapest-supplier risk, unclear ownership or sourcing decisions that may later need to be defended.</p><strong>Start with the Decision Blind Spot Starter Bundle</strong></a>
      <a class="route-card" href="#premium-review" title="Go to the Premium Review section"><span class="route-tag">Premium</span><h3>One decision already matters</h3><p>A defined supplier, contract, continuity or executive decision needs a written defensibility review.</p><strong>Go to Premium Review</strong></a>
      <a class="route-card" href="#product-the-contract-exposure-note"><span class="route-tag">Contracts</span><h3>Existing commitments are exposed</h3><p>Energy, freight, inflation, supplier capacity or customer pressure may be changing the economics of a contract.</p><strong>Choose Contract Exposure</strong></a>
      <a class="route-card" href="#product-decision-integrity-exposure-brief-when-one-update-stops-the-world"><span class="route-tag">Technology</span><h3>Digital supplier dependency</h3><p>A technology supplier, software update, ERP/MRP dependency or service interruption may become executive exposure.</p><strong>Choose CrowdStrike Brief</strong></a>
      <a class="route-card" href="#licensing" title="Go to formal licensing inquiry"><span class="route-tag">Institutional</span><h3>Implementation or enterprise use</h3><p>Training, dashboards, software, workflows, AI/LLM ingestion, ERP/MRP integration or organisational deployment require formal written licensing.</p><strong>Request licensed access</strong></a>
    </div>
    <p class="choice-rule"><strong>Rule:</strong> do not browse every product first. Select the closest exposure, buy the smallest adequate public-layer product, then move upward only if the decision risk justifies it.</p>
  </div>
</section>

