<div class="commercial-panel" id="start-here-by-role">
<p class="eyebrow">Start Here by Role</p>
<h2>Choose the product by responsibility, not by catalogue size.</h2>
<p>The fastest route is to start with the decision exposure closest to the reader's role. This reduces choice overload and moves the buyer toward the correct first product.</p>
<div class="conversion-choice-grid">
<div class="conversion-choice-card"><span class="role-label">CPO / Procurement</span><h3>Supplier, price or emergency buying exposure</h3><p>Begin with the practical entry route for procurement exposure before moving into deeper supplier or contract products.</p><a class="btn btn-gold" href="#product-decision-blind-spot-starter-bundle">Start with Decision Blind Spot Starter Bundle</a></div>
<div class="conversion-choice-card"><span class="role-label">Board / Executive</span><h3>One decision may later need to be defended</h3><p>Begin with board consequence or move directly to the premium written review when a defined exposure already matters.</p><a class="btn btn-gold" href="#premium-review">Request written review path</a></div>
<div class="conversion-choice-card"><span class="role-label">Contracts / Legal</span><h3>Existing commitments are exposed by external pressure</h3><p>Begin with contract exposure when freight, energy, supplier capacity, inflation or customer obligations change the economics of a commitment.</p><a class="btn btn-gold" href="#product-the-contract-exposure-note">Choose Contract Exposure Note</a></div>
<div class="conversion-choice-card"><span class="role-label">Supplier Risk</span><h3>Weak supplier signals are becoming visible</h3><p>Begin where supplier weakness may become delay, emergency buying, continuity failure, contract pressure or reputation exposure.</p><a class="btn btn-gold" href="#product-supplier-failure-before-impact">Go to Supplier Failure Before Impact</a></div>
<div class="conversion-choice-card"><span class="role-label">IT / ERP / Digital</span><h3>Technology dependency creates operational exposure</h3><p>Begin with the CrowdStrike case brief or the Technology Transformation Shift when software, digital services or ERP/MRP decisions carry consequence.</p><a class="btn btn-gold" href="#product-decision-integrity-exposure-brief-when-one-update-stops-the-world">Choose CrowdStrike Brief</a></div>
<div class="conversion-choice-card"><span class="role-label">Institutional Use</span><h3>The organisation wants capability, not only reading</h3><p>Books and products explain the problem. Implementation, software, training, workflows and institutional use require formal written licensing.</p><a class="btn btn-outline" href="#licensing">Request institutional access</a></div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="commercial-panel" id="buying-route">
<p class="eyebrow">Commercial Route</p>
<h2>Four levels. One controlled path.</h2>
<p>This site now separates first reading, deeper bundles, premium written assessment and formal institutional access so the visitor can choose without scanning the entire catalogue.</p>
<div class="product-ladder">
<div class="ladder-step"><strong>1. Entry</strong><span>€5.90–€24.90 briefings and starter products for immediate public-layer awareness.</span></div>
<div class="ladder-step"><strong>2. Bundles</strong><span>€49.90–€159.90 structured collections for wider domain understanding.</span></div>
<div class="ladder-step"><strong>3. Premium Review</strong><span>€2,500 written assessment of one defined decision, supplier, contract or continuity exposure.</span></div>
<div class="ladder-step"><strong>4. Licensing</strong><span>Formal written institutional access for implementation, software, training, workflows, dashboards, APIs or ERP/MRP integration.</span></div>
</div>
<p class="selection-note"><strong>Recommended first commercial product:</strong> for most procurement and supplier-exposure visitors, begin with the Decision Blind Spot Starter Bundle. For a defined live exposure, go directly to the Executive Decision Defensibility Review.</p>
</div>
<div class="commercial-panel" id="safe-preview">
