<h2>What the public layer gives the reader.</h2>
<div class="safe-preview"><p><strong>Public products provide:</strong> sharper language, clearer exposure questions, decision-record awareness and a structured way to see evidence, ownership, authority, options and consequence before pressure appears.</p><p><strong>They do not provide:</strong> implementation systems, internal operating templates, software logic, dashboards, workflow design, ERP/MRP integration, training rights or protected architecture.</p></div>
</div>

<section class="panel premium-review" id="premium-review" style="padding:clamp(1.4rem,3vw,3rem);margin-bottom:2rem">
<p class="eyebrow">Premium Written Review</p>
<h2>Executive Decision Defensibility Review</h2>
<p><strong>For leaders who already have one supplier, contract, continuity or procurement decision that may later be challenged.</strong></p>
<p>Premium written executive review for one defined decision, supplier exposure, contract position or continuity-risk situation. This is not a public briefing: it is a paid written assessment of a specific exposure, delivered as a PDF after accepted intake and receipt of agreed non-confidential information.</p>
<p class="premium-price-line">€2,500 · Written PDF · 5 business days</p>

<div class="premium-clarity-grid">
