<div class="premium-clarity-card"><strong>When to use it</strong><span>Use this when a real decision, supplier, contract or continuity-risk situation already matters enough to require written judgement rather than general reading.</span></div>
<div class="premium-clarity-card"><strong>What it is not</strong><span>Not legal advice, not consultancy deployment, not software, not training, not organisational implementation and not a substitute for formal institutional licensing.</span></div>
</div>

<p class="premium-urgency-line"><strong>Start before the decision becomes harder to defend.</strong> The review is for situations where consequence, scrutiny or accountability may later require a clear written position.</p>

